/target
img.jpg
.env
__pycache__/
.venv
venv/
.coverage
AGENTS.md
*.jpg

# Working notes kept on disk for back-checking, not repo content.
# PR1_WEB_GUI_LOG.md is the log for the web-GUI PR (#115); it records
# what was tried, what broke and why, which is useful when auditing that
# work but is not something the repository should carry.
PR1_WEB_GUI_LOG.md
PHASE1_LOG.md
PLAN.md
PROGRESS_LOG.md
# PR and issue drafts: text meant to live on GitHub once the PR or issue
# is opened, not as a permanent tracked file that would survive a squash
# merge into main. Globs rather than one line per draft, because the list
# only ever grows and a missed entry is how one gets committed by accident.
PR_*.md
ISSUE_*.md

# Local gprinterp path override (see .cargo/config.toml)
.cargo/
gprinterp/

# Scratch space for trying things on real data: old datasets kept around
# for comparison, and whatever the last command happened to write. These
# run to hundreds of megabytes, which GitHub refuses outright -- so until
# now the only thing stopping them being committed was noticing, and twice
# that was not enough.
tmp/
old/
/out.nc

# Processed radargrams dropped in the repo root while trying something on
# real data. These are tens of megabytes each and belong in tmp/ or
# outside the repo; two of them reached a remote branch because a
# `git add -A` swept up what a `git status` had shown as untracked.
# Ignoring the shape rather than the names, since the next one will be
# called something else.
/*.nc
